Theme and translation utilities are adapted from the Omarchy App Templates,
based on Omacut and Monologue (MIT, Copyright David Heinemeier Hansson).

Omarchy Terminal adapts the Bibata Original 2.0.7 arrow for its primary pointer
and the cursors with arrow badges (GPL-3.0-only, see COPYING-Bibata and NOTICE
within each theme). The other cursor artwork is original to Cursora under the
MIT license. The generator is in src/omarchycursor.cpp.

Bundled third-party cursor packs:
Bibata Modern and Original 2.0.7, by ful1e5 and contributors — GPL-3.0-only
https://github.com/ful1e5/Bibata_Cursor
BreezeX 2.0.1, by ful1e5 and contributors — GPL-3.0-only
https://github.com/ful1e5/BreezeX_Cursor
Phinger 2.2, by phisch and contributors — CC-BY-SA-4.0
https://github.com/phisch/phinger-cursors

Banana 2.0.0, by ful1e5 and contributors — GPL-3.0-only
https://github.com/ful1e5/banana-cursor
DMZ 0.4.5.2, copyright 2007–2010 Novell, Inc. — CC-BY-SA-3.0
https://sources.debian.org/src/dmz-cursor-theme/0.4.5.2/

Modifications by Cursora contributors (2026): rename bundled themes, convert
colored pixels to grayscale, and add modern cursor aliases to DMZ.
Shape geometry, alpha, sizes, hotspots, animation frames and timing are retained.
Each theme includes its upstream license in COPYING and attribution in NOTICE.
Corresponding upstream sources and the preparation/modification code are shipped
in /usr/share/cursora/sources; pinned source URLs and SHA-256 hashes are recorded
in vendor/sources.json. The utility code itself remains under the MIT license.
